  "summary": "College Station City Council voted 4-2 to renew its contract with Flock Safety, keeping 84 license plate readers operating for another year at nearly $400,000 annually. The vote followed nearly three hours of public comment overwhelmingly opposed to renewal, and some council members who voted yes said they would push for guardrails such as an independent audit and fewer cameras.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "College Station City Council voted 4-2 Thursday night to renew the city's contract with Flock Safety, keeping the city's network of 84 license plate reading cameras in operation.",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "The problem is the vendor's open architecture, their initial lack of concern for privacy in its initial design, and the company itself. Flock collects too much. It shares with too many. It uses inflexible contract language and marketing doublespeak.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "Cities across Texas have moved in the opposite direction in recent months, with several municipalities, including Bastrop, Robinson and Manvel, canceling or declining to renew their own Flock contracts",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
